message.content:
Sure! Below is a minimal example of an **interactive rotating card** using only HTML & CSS (no JavaScript).  
When you hover over the card, it smoothly rotates around its Y‑axis.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- Container ----------
   Keeps perspective so the rotation looks 3D */
.card-wrapper {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    margin: 50px auto;          /* center horizontally */
    perspective: 800px;         /* depth effect */
}

/* ---------- Card ----------
   The element that actually rotates */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* allow children to be positioned in 3D space */
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;/* smooth animation */
    cursor: pointer;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate 180° around Y axis */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* ---------- Front & Back Faces ----------
   Both occupy same space but are positioned back-to-front */
.front,
.back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide backside when rotated away */
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* Front face styling */
.front {
    background: #fff;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #333;
}

/* Back face styling – rotated 180° so it shows after flip */
.back {
    background: #fafafa;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* start flipped */
    padding: 20px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: #555;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="front">
            <span>Front Side</span>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="back">
            <h3>Back Side Content</h3>
            <p>This is some extra information that appears after the card flips.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a 3D perspective (`perspective`) so the rotation feels realistic. |
| `.card` | Holds both faces; `transform-style: preserve-3d` allows child elements to maintain their 3D positions. |
| `.front`, `.back` | Each occupies the same space. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the side facing away from the viewer. |
| `.back` | Initially rotated 180° (`rotateY(180deg)`) so it's hidden until the parent `.card` rotates. |
| `.card:hover` | Triggers the rotation with a smooth transition. |

Feel free to replace the content inside `.front` and `.back` with images, icons, or any other markup you like. Adjust the dimensions, colors, or transition duration to fit your design. Happy coding!
